ly bad coaching  decisions  yeah and the decision that ended up  being the the worst one  and vic fangio seemed to acknowledge  after the game that  maybe he shouldn't have done it today he  doubled down on the decision he made  down by three points 1916 six minutes  and 13 seconds remaining in the game  facing fourth and three on their own 49  they opted not to go for it they opted  to punt  and when you see look throw aside  analytics  and and this isn't meant to disrespect  the analytics crowd for me there's one  factor  that rises above all others when it  comes to analytics  are you keeping patrick mahomes on the  sideline yes or no  okay if you go for it and you get it  yes he's on the sidelines if you punt it  he's on the field and we've all seen  that patrick mahomes is a different guy  when the game's on the line when it's  time to go do it you know we all have  that moment there are different times in  our lives whether it's at work or if  there's a personal issue  we accept now's the time to go take care  of business and i think the chiefs are  that team more than any other in the nfl  that i can remember in years where  they'll just kind of coast and just kind  of coast and it's like okay it's time to  take care of business you gotta you  gotta understand that as a football  coach so  uh you you well we gotta make a stop  well yeah you gotta make a stop but it's  the chiefs it'd be different if it was  the chargers or if it was the jets or if  it was some other team and i know these  analytics formulas sharing are getting  more complex and they take those things  into account but  i have no faith in any analytics formula  that dictates that you should give the  ball back to patrick mahomes in a spot  where he's likely to along with his  teammates know it's time to go to work  yeah mike two things on this one i'm  wondering how much vic fangio being a  defensive minded coach played into this  i would think that a more offensive  minded coach would have wanted the ball  in the hands of his offense rather than  putting it on his defense to stop  patrick mahomes and so i do wonder if if  vic fangio being a defensive mind who  coached that played into his thinking  and the second thing is i think it would  have done a lot for drew locke even if  they don't make it if you go to drew  lock whether you call timeout or  whatever but you say look we're gonna  trust you to pick up this this first  down we're gonna put the ball in your  hands we're putting it on you to win  this game and you know what if they had  made that and gone on to have won this  game that could have really been a  turning point for drew lock and this  team but they didn't and they didn't  give him that chance and now you have to  wonder to through lock second guess  himself saying well they don't trust me  enough in that situation to put the ball  in my hands so you had an opportunity  there to do something for drew lock and  i think you failed drew luck by not  giving him a chance again you're a four  win team go for it do what you have to  do to try to win the game and give your  team some momentum going into 2021.  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports

